From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: reject unrepresentable NPU TX lengths

The NPU TX descriptor has a 13-bit packet length. FIELD_PREP silently
truncates a larger variable length, so an oversized monitor-injected MPDU
can be published with a different length from the skb/DMA mapping. Monitor
interfaces deliberately have no maximum MTU in mac80211.

Validate the final skb length after optional header padding, before DMA
mapping or tx_prepare_skb takes TX token ownership. Reuse the existing
TXWI/error cleanup and report EMSGSIZE. Leave the ordinary DMA path's
length handling unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
--- a/dma.c
+++ b/dma.c
@@ -708,6 +708,12 @@
 	if (dev->drv->drv_flags & MT_DRV_TX_ALIGNED4_SKBS)
 		mt76_insert_hdr_pad(skb);
 
+	if (mt76_npu_device_active(dev) &&
+	    skb->len > FIELD_MAX(NPU_TX_DMA_DESC_LEN_MASK)) {
+		ret = -EMSGSIZE;
+		goto free;
+	}
+
 	len = skb_headlen(skb);
 	addr = dma_map_single(dev->dma_dev, skb->data, len, DMA_TO_DEVICE);
 	if (unlikely(dma_mapping_error(dev->dma_dev, addr)))
